diff --git a/src/main/resources/assets/palaneogenesis/lang/en_us.json b/src/main/resources/assets/palaneogenesis/lang/en_us.json
index 1fe06fb..20ddd90 100644
--- a/src/main/resources/assets/palaneogenesis/lang/en_us.json
+++ b/src/main/resources/assets/palaneogenesis/lang/en_us.json
@@ -24,5 +24,37 @@
     "book.palaneogenesis.category.items.name": "Items",
     "book.palaneogenesis.category.items.description": "Every item added by the mod, what it does, and how to craft it.",
     "book.palaneogenesis.category.effects.name": "Effects",
-    "book.palaneogenesis.category.effects.description": "Coming soon."
+    "book.palaneogenesis.category.effects.description": "Coming soon.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page1": "Long before the powers known today existed, villages lived under the protection of ancient guardians. Káak Tun was one of them.$(br2)For years he protected primitive villages as the world slowly fell into chaos, watching wars, invasions, and creatures that drove the old peoples from their homes.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page2": "The Nether became a threat. The End became a threat. And the villages he had sworn to protect disappeared, one by one.$(br2)Káak Tun remained. Time turned the warrior into an elder, but it could never take his strength or his wisdom from him.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page3": "Now he has returned. He dwells among the villages once more, still keeping the oath he made centuries ago: to protect them.$(br2)But Káak Tun understands something the old warriors never could - the power of the past is no longer alone. Something from the future has begun to meet it, and Steve stands right in the middle of that convergence.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page4": "A tireless guardian. Wherever a village stands, a Káak Tun is never far - watching over it exactly as he always has.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page5": "Despite his imposing size, Káak Tun never attacks the player - not even in retaliation if struck first. His only enemies are the hostile creatures that threaten the village he guards.$(br2)With 300 health and armor to match a full set of diamond, he is far tougher than an Iron Golem, and just as unshakeable in his purpose.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page6": "Once a hostile mob draws near, Káak Tun answers with two attacks: a heavy melee strike at close range, and a charged beam fired at anything within reach after a couple of seconds spent taking aim.$(br2)The melee blow is deliberately the stronger of the two - Káak Tun always prefers to finish a fight up close.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.mobs.kaak_tun.page7": "A Blue Heart can be earned from Káak Tun in two ways. The peaceful route: feed him Lapis Lazuli - four offerings are rewarded with a single heart, freely given.$(br2)The other way is combat: since Káak Tun never strikes first, any battle is a choice the player makes - and defeating him always leaves a Blue Heart behind.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.blue_heart.page1": "The Blue Heart represents the ancient guardians: simple, resilient warriors determined to remain standing.$(br2)They needed no extraordinary powers. Their greatest virtue was endurance - taking one blow, then another, and continuing to advance.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.blue_heart.page2": "The Blue Heart carries that legacy: the strength of those who didn't need to defeat the enemy quickly. They only needed to survive it.$(br2)While transformed, using a Blue Heart grants a small amount of temporary life - and nothing else. No duration, no side effects: it's the most basic safeguard the ancient power offers.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.blue_heart.page3": "Blue Hearts are earned from $(l:mobs/kaak_tun)Káak Tun$() - offered peacefully in exchange for Lapis Lazuli, or left behind after a fight.$(br2)They have no crafting recipe of their own, but every other heart in this guide - and the Ancient Extract Syringe itself - requires at least one to create.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.empty_syringe.page1": "The Empty Syringe serves two purposes. Combined with the right ingredients, it becomes the base for an Ancient Extract Syringe - but once the player is transformed, using an Empty Syringe on its own ends the transformation instead.$(br2)Reverting shatters the syringe: what remains afterward is a $(l:items/broken_syringe)Broken Syringe$().",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.ancient_extract_syringe.title_recipe": "How It's Made",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.ancient_extract_syringe.page1": "This is where the transformation begins. Injecting the Ancient Extract Syringe channels the power of the past directly into Steve's body.$(br2)The change is immediate: maximum health collapses to a single half-heart, but in its place Steve gains a reserve of temporary life - the same currency stored in every Blue Heart - along with a lasting boost to speed and attack strength for as long as the transformation holds.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.ancient_extract_syringe.page2": "Unlike most items in this guide, the Ancient Extract Syringe isn't made at a crafting table. An $(l:items/empty_syringe)Empty Syringe$() is dipped in a source of Water together with Lapis Lazuli, Blackstone, and a $(l:items/blue_heart)Blue Heart$() to complete the process.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.ancient_extract_syringe.page3": "Transforming and reverting back and forth too quickly comes at a cost: toggling five times within a few seconds permanently costs Steve one full heart of maximum health, though it can never fall below one whole heart.$(br2)To revert safely, use an $(l:items/empty_syringe)Empty Syringe$() while transformed.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.broken_syringe.page1": "What's left of an $(l:items/empty_syringe)Empty Syringe$() after it's used to end a transformation - a spent, shattered shell rather than a reusable container.$(br2)It can't be refilled or used for anything else. A fresh Empty Syringe has to be crafted before the ancient power can be channeled again.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.explosive_heart.page1": "Some warriors knew perfectly well that they could die - and fought anyway. For them, death didn't mean leaving the battle. It meant turning their final instant into a weapon.$(br2)Many would have called them kamikazes. Those waiting for them back home called them heroes.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.explosive_heart.page2": "The Explosive Heart carries that sacrifice. While transformed, using one grants a small amount of temporary life, same as any other heart - but when a point of it breaks in combat, it detonates around Steve, destroying nearby hostile mobs without damaging a single block.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.resistance_heart.page1": "Other warriors understood that resisting didn't simply mean enduring. Every battle made them stronger; every blow prepared them for the next.$(br2)The warriors of the resistance advanced as their bodies and their will adapted to war itself.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.resistance_heart.page2": "A single Resistance Heart alone grants only a modest edge. But as more points build up at once, its passive effect grows with them - resistance gradually turning into raw mining speed - and breaking a point grants a burst of Resistance.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.inverted_heart.page1": "And there were those who received something no warrior should ever have carried: a malevolent power, capable of consuming them from within.$(br2)They refused to let it decide their fate. Instead of being destroyed by it, they did the impossible - they inverted their own heart. What should have destroyed them became what would destroy their enemies instead.",
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.inverted_heart.page2": "The Inverted Heart has no active effect of its own. But when a point of it breaks, it drains the life from every hostile creature for a huge distance around Steve - sparing only the Ender Dragon - striking each one down with a burst of ash and soul rather than an explosion.",
+
+    "book.palaneogenesis.entry.items.kaak_tun_spawn_egg.page1": "A standard spawn egg for $(l:mobs/kaak_tun)Káak Tun$(), available only in Creative mode.$(br2)It has no crafting recipe - it exists purely to place a guardian directly, rather than waiting for one to appear near a village."
 }
